## 4. Commercial Boundaries

The source-available grant is intended for internal review, evaluation,
development, testing, training, and self-hosted Community use. A separate
written agreement with Tessallite is required to:

- sell, sublicense, rent, lease, distribute, or transfer the Covered Source or
  modified versions to a third party;
- provide Tessallite, the Covered Source, modified versions, or derivative works
  as a hosted, managed, bureau, resale, OEM, white-label, embedded, or
  service-provider offering to third parties;
- use the Covered Source to build or offer a competing commercial semantic
  layer, BI gateway, analytics platform, managed service, or substantially
  similar product;
- publish, share, or distribute patches, forks, builds, images, or packages that
  include Proprietary Components or Tessallite proprietary material.

You agree to keep copyright, trademark, proprietary, and license notices in
place; use Tessallite names, logos, domains, marks, and brand assets only as
allowed by written brand guidance; use signed-license and entitlement controls
as provided; and not reverse engineer, decompile, disassemble, or attempt to
extract source code from Proprietary Components except to the extent mandatory
